From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: what XAML-Islands installer dialogs use

TeraCopy's downloaded installer (an Advanced Installer bootstrapper whose dialogs are XAML in an island) showed no window: its dialog creation stopped at the first class or member we did not have and then crashed in its own loop. With the XAML switch of 6131 its whole flow now works -- the "Install TeraCopy?" page, Install and its Configure menu, the per-user/everybody page, the folder page, the progress page, and TeraCopy launched when ready. Added for it: a default Application when the thread's XAML is initialized, the application's Resources falling back on the framework's, UIElement.XamlRoot and FocusManager.GetFocusedElement(XamlRoot), VisualTreeHelper, Canvas, UIElement.Transitions with ScalarTransition, PaneThemeTransition and the theme transitions (kept, not animated), VisualStateManager statics, Windows.UI.Text.FontWeights, KeyboardAccelerators, ToggleButton, CheckBox, RadioButton (parent and GroupName groups), SplitButton (primary part and chevron), MenuFlyout with MenuFlyoutItem/MenuFlyoutSeparator, RangeBase, ProgressBar and ProgressRing, and Image sources given as file names.
---
